OL,3,GNEWSASwim challenge 'error' leaves man
OL,4,Abarely able to walk
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man said he could "hardly walk" after
OL,7,Fcompleting a long distance cold water
OL,8,Fswim following his wife's keyboard
OL,9,Ferror.
OL,11,FMike Thorpe, 57, from Fyfield in
OL,12,FWiltshire, was planning to swim one
OL,13,Fmile (1.6km) in the Swim Serpentine at
OL,14,FHyde Park in London, but was forced to
OL,15,Fswim an extra five miles (8km) after
OL,16,Fhis wife hit the wrong button.
OL,18,FSusanna Thorpe said her husband's
OL,19,Fachievement was "amazing", but she
OL,20,Fwould not be forgiven "for a very long
OL,21,Ftime".
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,350,340,200,160,0,100
